~ start

if GameState.get_flag("level_4_completed", false)
	=> stage_post_4
elif GameState.get_flag("level_3_completed", false)
	=> stage_post_3
elif GameState.get_flag("level_2_completed", false)
	=> stage_post_2
elif GameState.get_flag("level_1_completed", false)
	=> stage_post_1
elif GameState.get_flag("dialtone_greeted", false)
	=> stage_nudge

=> stage_intro

# ── Intro — first hub talk, before Level 1 ───────────────────────────────

~ stage_intro

DialTone: Hey — over here.
do Cutscene.show_video("res://cutscenes/dialtone_intro.ogv")
DialTone: Name's DialTone.
DialTone: Listen — my friend Nyx is stuck between sectors. Need you to break her loose.
=> dialtone_questions

~ stage_nudge

DialTone: Hey — time's ticking.
=> dialtone_questions


# Single shared question hub. Both stage_intro and stage_nudge dump into
# this menu. Each option contains its own inline mini-dialogue, then
# falls through to the => dialtone_questions loop at the bottom so the
# menu re-shows. Visited-dim handles "what have I asked?" via the
# existing balloon hooks. The exit option text swaps based on whether
# the player has been greeted yet (sets dialtone_greeted in intro_done).

~ dialtone_questions

# [#decision] for the dim walker: the hacker question below is a one-shot
# fork (gated away on re-picks), so one visit answers the probe.
- Are you who messaged me? [#decision]
	DialTone: ...perhaps.
	DialTone: Let's just say I noticed you. The way you asked questions on Hacker News intrigued me.
	DialTone: I wanted to see what you were made of.
	# VECTOR — commitment read on the player's intent, mirrors Nyx's post-1
	# "you actually want to be a hacker?" (nyx_trust). One-shot: re-picks of
	# the probe skip the question so the nudge can't stack.
	if GameState.get_flag("dialtone_messenger_thread", 0) == 0
		DialTone: You do want to become a **real** hacker right?
		- Yes [#vector]
			DialTone: Well, I need you to help my friend first.
			do StoryVec.nudge(&"dialtone_trust", 1)
		- Thinking about it [#vector]
			DialTone: Don't think too long.
		do GameState.set_flag("dialtone_messenger_thread", 1)
- Who's Nyx?
	DialTone: Nyx. Sharpest hacker on the grid and she's stuck. Don't ask me how.
	do GameState.set_flag("dialtone_asked_nyx", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("dialtone_asked_nyx", false) /] What am I looking for down there?
	DialTone: Her signal. Drifting in the static — flickering between sectors. You'll know it when you see it.
	do GameState.set_flag("dialtone_asked_looking", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("dialtone_asked_looking", false) /] Why can't you go yourself?
	DialTone: Local node's flagged to my address. I jack in from here, it alerts **the authorities**. No joke.
	DialTone: You're a clean IP — you can slip right through.
- [if !GameState.get_flag("dialtone_greeted", false) /] I'm in. Where's the portal? [#exit]
	=> intro_done
- [if GameState.get_flag("dialtone_greeted", false) /] That's all. [#exit]
	=> intro_done
=> dialtone_questions


~ intro_done

# Smart exit. First time through (not yet greeted): hand off the walkie,
# set the unlocks, advance the arc. Re-entry from stage_nudge: short
# nudge line and out.
if GameState.get_flag("dialtone_greeted", false)
	DialTone: Portal's right there, runner. Nyx isn't getting any more un-trapped.
	=> END

DialTone: Take this — walkie's on my channel. I'll be in your ear the whole run.
DialTone: Portal's right behind me. Step on, press enter, you're in.
DialTone: Go bring her back.
do GameState.add_item("walkie_talkie")
do GameState.set_flag("walkie_talkie_owned", true)
do GameState.set_flag("dialtone_greeted", true)
do GameState.set_flag("level_1_unlocked", true)
=> END

# ── Post Level 1 — prank reveal ──────────────────────────────────────────

~ stage_post_1

# Obligatory opener — runs once. Re-talks route through the entry block
# for an abbreviated greeting, then drop into the questions hub.
if GameState.get_flag("post_1_opener_seen", false)
	=> post_1_entry

DialTone: Ha  ha — look who's back!
Nyx: How many times have you pulled that same stunt, really? Does it not get old for you?
DialTone: Never gets old.
Nyx: It does. Trust me.
do GameState.set_flag("post_1_opener_seen", true)
=> post_1_questions


# Re-talk greeting. Fires once per dialogue session because the questions
# hub self-loops to itself, never back to entry.

~ post_1_entry

DialTone: What else would you like to know?
=> post_1_questions


# Single shared question hub. "Back to those questions you mentioned"
# is a flag-gated follow-up that requires both having heard the prank
# explanation AND having asked DialTone earlier (dialtone_messenger_thread=1).

~ post_1_questions

- So what was that about?
	DialTone: Come on. Nyx? Stuck?
	DialTone: She's the best there is! I just wanted to see both of your faces.
	Nyx: You're an idiot.
	DialTone: Completely worth it.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_1_asked_explain", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_1_asked_explain", false) and GameState.get_flag("dialtone_messenger_thread", 0) == 1 /] Back to those questions you mentioned…
	DialTone: Oh, **those**. Yeah. Spent a few weeks just lurking.
	DialTone: You had a particular flavor — kept asking what nobody else was asking. Wanted to see what you were made of.
	do GameState.set_flag("dialtone_messenger_thread", 2)
- So what's next? [#exit]
	=> post_1_done
=> post_1_questions


~ post_1_done

DialTone: Alright — got the next job queued. Softball, this time. Real one. Grab a few files for us and you will be back here in no time.
# VECTOR — post-prank commitment read; nudges dialtone_trust. One-shot:
# post_1_done re-runs on every exit until level 2 completes, so the flag
# keeps DialTone from re-asking and the nudge from stacking.
if !GameState.get_flag("post_1_hacker_commit", false)
	DialTone: You do still want to be a hacker right?
	- Not after that [#vector]
		Nyx: I don't blame you.
		DialTone: Come on. It's all in good fun.
		Nyx: Is it?
		do StoryVec.nudge(&"dialtone_trust", -1)
	- Sure [#vector]
		DialTone: That's the spirit!
		do StoryVec.nudge(&"dialtone_trust", 1)
	do GameState.set_flag("post_1_hacker_commit", true)
DialTone: This is the easiest hop on the grid.
Nyx: Runner, over here if you have a moment.
do GameState.set_flag("level_2_unlocked", true)
=> END

# ── Post Level 2 — Splice surfaces, near miss ────────────────────────────

~ stage_post_2

# Obligatory opener — runs once. Re-talks route through the entry block
# for an abbreviated greeting, then drop into the questions hub.
if GameState.get_flag("post_2_opener_seen", false)
	=> post_2_entry

DialTone: {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}. You made it back.
Nyx: He wouldn't have made it back if I wasn't there to pull him out.
DialTone: Well, that's true.
DialTone: The good news is you are officially a hacker.
DialTone: The bad news is Splice is on your trail.
DialTone: And he tipped his hand. He's hunting something.
DialTone: A power-up. The kind that opens a door to the next door.
DialTone: If he gets all the way down? Root. After that the Gibson is his and the rest of us are gone.
Nyx: Hackers as a thing — done.
- What do we do?
	DialTone: We find it first.
do GameState.set_flag("post_2_opener_seen", true)
=> post_2_questions


# Re-talk greeting. Fires once per dialogue session because the questions
# hub self-loops to itself, never back to entry.

~ post_2_entry

DialTone: You got the plan?
=> post_2_questions


# Single shared question hub. Inline mini-dialogues per option, with
# flag-gated follow-ups ("Run is putting it lightly?" off the Splice probe;
# "Vague." off the target probe) per Rule 6 progressive revelation. Loops
# back via trailing => post_2_questions; "I'm in." exits to post_2_done.

~ post_2_questions

# WORLD-BUILD — the stakes: what Splice controlling the Gibson costs everyone.
- Why does it matter?
	DialTone: You're kind of thick aren't you?
	Nyx: If Splice controls the Gibson, thats the end of the Grid soon after.
	DialTone: Do you like being able to host your own e-sites, play free games, write a blog? All that is history without paying a platform fee and ads shoved in your face once Splice is in control.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_2_asked_matter", true)
# WORLD-BUILD — Splice history reveal: who he is. Rule 6 progressive
# revelation — unlocks after the stakes probe above. Ends on Nyx shutting
# the thread down; pulling it further is the follow-up probe below.
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_2_asked_matter", false) /] Who is Splice?
	Nyx: Don't.
	DialTone: He's going to find out sooner or later
	Nyx: Fine.
	Nyx: We used to run with Splice.
	DialTone: Run is putting it lightly.
	Nyx: Shut up.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_2_asked_who", true)
# WORLD-BUILD — the end-game reveal, with a flavor reaction beat. Rule 6 —
# pulls the thread Nyx just shut down, so it only opens after the probe above.
# [#decision] here is for the dim walker: the reaction fork is pick-one
# flavor, so one visit answers the probe (it dims without exhausting both).
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_2_asked_who", false) /] And how do you know what he wants? [#decision]
	DialTone: We know his end game. Hell, he almost convinced us.
	DialTone: He called it "an opportunity".
	Nyx: An opportunity to make massive profit margins and at the same time irrevocably pollute the biggest innovation since electricity - This place.
	- That's horrible [#vector]
		DialTone: You can say that again
		do StoryVec.nudge(&"humanity", 1)
		- That's horrible [#vector]
			do StoryVec.nudge(&"humanity", 1)
		Nyx: Dude, you are so weird.
	- Sounds dope [#vector]
		Nyx: DialTone, what are we even doing with this clown?
		do StoryVec.nudge(&"humanity", -1)
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_2_asked_who", false) /] Run is putting it lightly?
	DialTone: They were a thing.
	Nyx: Were. Past tense.
	DialTone: She doesn't like talking about it.
	Nyx: No.
- So what's the plan?
	DialTone: You and Nyx Split. Stay synced up on the channel.
	DialTone: Your portal's queued behind us.
	do GameState.set_flag("level_3_unlocked", true)
	do GameState.set_flag("post_2_asked_plan", true)
	Nyx: Splice will be hunting too. Move fast.
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_2_asked_plan", false) /] What am I looking for?
	DialTone: Honestly? Could be anything. A weird file, a route that shouldn't exist. You'll know it when it doesn't belong.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_2_asked_target", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_2_asked_target", false) /] Vague.
	Nyx: He doesn't know.
	DialTone: I genuinely don't.
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_2_asked_who", false) /] How did he get into the sentinels?
	DialTone: Sentinels are old code. He found a backdoor.
	Nyx: He made one.
	DialTone: Either way — they listen to him now.
- [if GameState.get_flag("dialtone_messenger_thread", 0) == 2 /] You said boards earlier.
	DialTone: The boards. Yeah.
	DialTone: Honestly? You can clearly run with the best of them.
	DialTone: If you want in, you're in.
	do GameState.set_flag("dialtone_messenger_thread", 3)
- I'm in. [#exit]
	=> post_2_done
=> post_2_questions


~ post_2_done

DialTone: Alright let's get moving runner.
Nyx: {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}. A word?
do GameState.set_flag("level_3_unlocked", true)
=> END

# ── Post Level 3 — loyal branch only (betray path exits to its own scene) ─

# CANON — the Nyx/DialTone argument, overheard as ambient in-room voice
# (Companion bus) on the player's first hub entry post-L3. Driven by the
# Post3Overheard CutsceneSequence in hub.tscn (background-dialogue mode:
# no cameras, no freeze, music untouched) — never reached from ~start
# routing. stage_post_3's opener ("How long were you standing there?")
# picks up face-to-face from here.

~ post_3_overheard

Nyx: We shouldn't have sent him in. That was too dangerous.
DialTone: But we got it. He got the disc.
Nyx: He almost didn't.
DialTone: He did, though.
Nyx: He was off the channel for ninety seconds. Splice had him in a room.
DialTone: And he walked out. With the disc.
Nyx: Because he said no. Not because of us. Because of him.
DialTone: ...yeah.
DialTone: ...yeah, that's true.
DialTone: We were sloppy. We owe him better.
Nyx: We can't do that again. We just **can't** 
Nyx: sorry. I'm sorry.
DialTone: ...nothing to be sorry about.
=> END

~ stage_post_3

# CANON — obligatory opener. The player overheard the argument
# (post_3_overheard above); this picks up face-to-face. Runs once.
# Re-talks route through the entry block for an abbreviated greeting,
# then drop into the questions hub.
if GameState.get_flag("post_3_opener_seen", false)
	=> post_3_entry

Nyx: How long were you standing there?
DialTone: We couldn't hear you two in there. Channel was dead.
DialTone: What did he say?
do GameState.set_flag("post_3_opener_seen", true)
=> post_3_questions


# Re-talk greeting. Fires once per dialogue session because the questions
# hub self-loops to itself, never back to entry.

~ post_3_entry

DialTone: What's up, {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}?
=> post_3_questions


# Single shared question hub. The plan reveal lives as one probe so the
# player has agency over when to hear it; if they exit via "I'm ready"
# without asking, post_3_done plays it as a forced reveal first.

~ post_3_questions

# Default debrief for the instant-refusal path — the player who shut Splice
# down before the pitch. Mutually exclusive with "Bitter. World-rigged..."
- [if not GameState.get_flag("splice_pitched", false) /] I didn't let him say much.
	DialTone: Ha! Good.
	Nyx: Nothing he says is worth hearing anyway.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_3_debriefed", true)
# Gated on having actually heard the pitch (splice_consider sets the flag;
# an instant "Get off my channel." skips it entirely).
- [if GameState.get_flag("splice_pitched", false) /] Bitter. World-rigged. He went on about being wronged.
	DialTone: heh. Splice always was like that. Even back when.
	Nyx: He's not wrong that the rules screwed him. He just thinks that means he gets to screw everyone else.
	DialTone: That tracks.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_3_asked_bitter", true)
	do GameState.set_flag("post_3_debriefed", true)
# Rule 6 progressive revelation — the personal thread only opens after the
# player has given the surface-level debrief above, AND only if Splice
# actually opened the Nyx thread in L3 (splice_nyx sets the flag; the door
# roll can fail, in which case this debrief never happened).
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_3_asked_bitter", false) and GameState.get_flag("splice_mentioned_nyx", false) /] It got personal. About Nyx.
	Nyx: ...yeah.
	Nyx: He's been doing that since I left.
	DialTone: We don't have to talk about that.
	Nyx: It's fine. He's wrong about whatever he said. Anyway.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_3_debriefed", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_3_debriefed", false) /] What's the plan now?
	DialTone: Splice showed his hand. He didn't mean to — he thought he'd already won.
	DialTone: That's our window.
	Nyx: He's cocky now. He'll take a bait we set.
	DialTone: We know where the last disc is. He doesn't know we know.
	DialTone: It's stack-locked. Only fires if you've got the disc you just brought back. You do. He doesn't know that either.
	Nyx: We don't know what it does.
	DialTone: But the breadcrumbs say it'll turn the tables.
	DialTone: We bait him. He walks in expecting another easy win. You hit him with whatever this thing is.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_3_plan_revealed", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("post_3_debriefed", false) /] I'm ready for the next one. [#exit]
	=> post_3_done
=> post_3_questions


~ post_3_done

# Forced plan reveal if the player skipped that probe. Idempotent; the
# flag also guards re-entry so this never plays twice.
if !GameState.get_flag("post_3_plan_revealed", false)
	DialTone: Before you go.
	DialTone: We know where the last disc is. Splice doesn't know we know.
	DialTone: It's stack-locked. Only fires if you've got the disc you just brought back.
	DialTone: We bait him. He walks in expecting another easy win. You hit him with whatever this thing is.
	do GameState.set_flag("post_3_plan_revealed", true)
DialTone: We've got him, runner.
DialTone: Last sector.
DialTone: **Your** call when we move.
Nyx: {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}, do you have a sec?
do GameState.set_flag("level_4_unlocked", true)
=> END

# ── Post Level 4 — loyal endgame (Splice quarantined, not destroyed) ─────

~ stage_post_4

# Obligatory opener — runs once. Re-talks route through post_4_entry for
# a warm greeting, then drop into the questions hub.
if GameState.get_flag("post_4_opener_seen", false)
	=> post_4_entry

DialTone: Splice is quarantined. Not gone — but boxed in. The grid's logging it everywhere.
DialTone: They're calling it "the Gibson run". You're a name now, {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}.
DialTone: ...the music's Nyx's call. I'm contractually dancing.
do GameState.set_flag("post_4_opener_seen", true)
=> post_4_questions


# Re-talk greeting. Fires once per dialogue session because post_4_questions
# self-loops to itself, never back to entry.

~ post_4_entry

DialTone: Hey {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}.
=> post_4_questions


# Single shared question hub.

~ post_4_questions

DialTone: Anything else?
- What now?
	DialTone: Honestly? You take a week off. Then we'll see who shows up at the channel.
- About Splice — he's still in there.
	DialTone: Quarantine holds as long as the perimeter does. Let's not talk about what happens if it doesn't.
- Sign me out. [#exit]
	=> post_4_done
=> post_4_questions


~ post_4_done

DialTone: Catch you around, runner.
do GameState.set_flag("game_completed", true)
=> END
